Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Abdurrahman Bulut
Author-Workplace-Name: Emekli Microsoft Projeler Koordinatörü
Title: Hanif Teknoloji: Dataist Distopyadan Fıtrat Medeniyeti’ne
Abstract: The industrialisation process that began in the 18th century has evolved into a new era in which technology, accelerating development over the last 20 years, has enveloped human life. Within this process, technology has not only made people's daily tasks easier, but has also begun to change their perception of existence (ontology) and values. Technology has now become the platform for a new sociology based on a dataist methodology of thinking. The singularity, predicted to occur by 2045, the third phase of artificial intelligence, and the advanced models of quantum computers raise the worrying question of what kind of world we will live in by the 2050s. Advances in science and technology over the last three centuries have brought unimaginable developments from production to communication; yet the same period has witnessed a sharp decline in fundamental values such as virtue, conscience, respect, family and decency. The replacement of metaphysical values by physical ones has become an observable, even tangible reality. Moreover, no technology developed during the industrial revolutions has left the ecosystem and human disposition (fitrah) unharmed. This article grounds the paradox between technological development and the erosion of human values in the context of the ontology-technology relationship and offers a prognosis of its causes. It argues for a new philosophy of technology and proposes the "Hanif Technology" concept (philosophy) based on divine unity (tawhid) and harmony with nature and human disposition (fitrah) as a solution.
Keywords: Philosophy of Technology, Hanif Technology, Ontology, Fitrah, Dataism, Artificial Intelligence
